></div></div><div fs-slider-element=\"scrollbar\" class=\"fs-slider-gallery_scrollbar\"><div fs-slider-element=\"scrollbar-drag\" class=\"fs-slider-gallery_scrollbar_drag\"></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class=\"faq-section\"><div class=\"w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container\"><div data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bc3\" class=\"header-faq\"><h2>Pergola Installation FAQs</h2><div>Have questions about custom aluminum pergola installation in Florida? Our licensed outdoor living specialists answer the top questions here.</div></div><div class=\"wrapper-faq-components\"><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bc7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Are aluminum pergolas rust-proof for Florida outdoor use?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Yes. Powder-coated aluminum pergolas resist rust, corrosion, and UV damage — making them ideal for Florida's humid, salt-air coastal environments and sun-intense inland climates. Licensed under aluminum contractor license SCC131153553, Mr. &amp; Mrs. Outdoor Living engineers every structure to local wind-load specifications.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bcf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Are aluminum pergolas better than wood in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Aluminum outperforms wood in Florida's demanding climate. Powder-coated aluminum resists rust, rot, insect damage, and UV fading without seasonal staining or resealing. Unlike wood, aluminum maintains its structural integrity in coastal humidity, salt air, and intense heat — delivering decades of reliable performance with minimal upkeep.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bd7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">How long does pergola installation take in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Most custom pergola installations are completed in one to three days once permits are approved and materials are fabricated. Timelines vary based on structural complexity and HOA review requirements. Our licensed team coordinates engineering, fabrication, and final inspection to ensure your Florida project stays on schedule.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bdf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Can a pergola reduce home cooling costs in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Yes. A strategically positioned pergola creates significant shade over windows, sliding doors, and patio areas — reducing solar heat gain on your Florida home. By limiting the sun's impact on glass and exterior walls, a well-placed pergola can help reduce air-conditioning use during South Florida's intense summer months.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077be7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Are permits required for outdoor projects in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Our pergola builders manage the complete permit process and ensure every installation meets Florida building codes and HOA or ARB design requirements. Licensed under SCC131153553, Mr. &amp; Mrs. Outdoor Living coordinates all inspections and approvals — so your project proceeds without delays and is structurally certified upon completion.</p></nav></div></div></div><img sizes=\"100vw\" srcset=\"/images/site/design2-p-500.webp 500w, /images/site/design2-p-800.webp 800w, /images/site/design2-p-1080.webp 1080w, /images/site/design2-p-1600.webp 1600w, /images/site/design2.webp 1920w\" alt=\"\" src=\"/images/site/design2.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"design-bg\" width=\"1920\" height=\"146\"></section></div><section class=\"location\"><div class=\"w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container\"><div data-w-id=\"dfdd7317-58e7-27b3-99a6-2c20a5e8a7be\" class=\"header-location\"><h2>Where We Serve</h2><p>Regional Coverage W